---
import Shell from '../layouts/shell.astro';
---

<Shell title="About — Skiddle" description="About Jeff (Skiddle) — platform engineer in Bangkok, homelabber, open-web fan and student pilot.">
  <div class="max-w-[70ch] w-full">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
      <img src="https://github.com/arcestia.png?size=160" alt="Jeff's avatar" width="72" height="72" class="size-18 rounded-full border shrink-0" />
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-semibold text-xl before-hash-1">About me</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-1">Platform engineer · Bangkok · night person</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm <strong>Jeff</strong>, known online as <strong>Skiddle</strong>. I work the night shift as a platform
        engineer in Bangkok: building platforms, automating ops, and keeping infrastructure running across cloud
        and my homelab.
      </p>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        Most days I'm working with <code>Go</code>, <code>PHP/Laravel</code>, <code>Node.js</code>,
        <code>Postgres</code>/<code>MariaDB</code>/<code>Redis</code> and <code>Docker</code>/<code>Kubernetes</code>,
        on <code>Cloudflare</code>, <code>AWS</code> and self-hosted hardware.
      </p>
      <p>
        I co-founded <strong>Aerialite</strong>, a security and privacy startup here in Bangkok, and now sit on its
        advisory board. I also run <strong>Skiddle ID</strong>, where I build web apps and look after infrastructure
        for clients. The full version is on my <a href="/works/">CV</a>, and the open-source bits are on
        <a href="/projects/">projects</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Automate the toil.</strong> A small tool beats doing the same manual step twice.</li>
        <li><strong>Reliability, security, cost.</strong> I weigh all three on every change, not just the first one.</li>
        <li><strong>Own your data.</strong> Open protocols and self-hosting, where it makes sense.</li>
        <li><strong>Share what I learn.</strong> I write up what I build here, including the parts that went wrong.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The open web</h2>
      <p>
        I care about open protocols and owning your own data. I'm into ATProto, I'm on Bluesky as
        <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/skiddle.blue" rel="me">@skiddle.blue</a>, and I run as much as I can myself.
        This site is where I write about what I'm building, what I'm learning, and sometimes things that have nothing to
        do with tech.
      </p>

      <h2>Outside of work</h2>
      <p>
        I have ADHD, and it doesn't stop me doing the work. I game, I read, and I keep odd hours. Right now I'm also
        working toward my Private Pilot License, and I'm <a href="/topics/tag/aviation/">writing about that journey</a> too.
      </p>
      <p>
        Curious what hardware and software I use? It's all on the <a href="/uses/">uses</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Say hi</h2>
      <p>
        For work: <a href="mailto:work@skiddle.id">work@skiddle.id</a>. For everything else:
        <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/skiddle.blue" rel="me">Bluesky</a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/arcestia" rel="me">GitHub</a> or
        <a href="mailto:jeff@skiddle.id">jeff@skiddle.id</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Shell>
